	"game:tabname-stonesupportbeam": "Stone Support Beams",

	"supportbeam-handbook-guide-title": "Crafting Guide",
	"supportbeam-handbook-guide-text": "See the full crafting process: <a href=\"handbook://stonesupportbeam:guide\">stone support beam: Crafting Guide</a>",

	"guide-title": "Crafting Mechanic: Stone support beams",
	"guide-text": "Building a stone support beam requires five separate crafting steps, each using a different existing game mechanic:\n\n1. Clay Mold — Shape clay using the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-clayforming\">clayforming</a> system into a raw mold, then fire it in a pit or <a href=\"handbook://gamemechanicinfo-beehivekiln\">beehive kiln</a>. The mold is reusable; it won't be consumed when crafting the final beam, only slowly worn down with use.\n\n2. <a href=\"handbook://item-stonesupportbeam:crushedstone-granite\">Crushed Stone</a> (or <a href=\"handbook://item-stonesupportbeam:crushedbrick-granite\">Crushed Brick</a> for ashlar variants) — Hammer raw stone (or an ashlar brick) on the crafting grid to crush it down.\n\n3. <a href=\"handbook://item-stonesupportbeam:stonebeam-concretemix-granite\">Rubble Concrete</a> — Start by mixing water and lime in a barrel to make <a href=\"handbook://item-limewaterportion\">limewater</a>. Add sand of your chosen stone support beam type (limestone sand for any marble variants, and for halite, kimberlite and obsidian, which have no sand of their own) to make a <a href=\"handbook://item-stonesupportbeam:cementmix-graniteportion\">lime slurry</a>. Finally, add crushed stone (or crushed brick, for ashlar variants) matching the sand type of the slurry and seal the barrel for 48 in-game hours to cure it into rubble concrete. The sand and crushed stone/brick must be matching in variant (e.g. granite sand with granite crushed stone), and ashlar variants require crushed brick specifically — regular crushed stone won't produce an ashlar style concrete and stone support beam.\n\n4. <a href=\"handbook://item-stonesupportbeam:rebar-iron\">Iron Cramp</a> — Forged from iron ingot at an anvil.\n\n5. Final Assembly — Combine the rubble concrete, iron cramp, and fired clay mold in the crafting grid to produce the finished stone support beam. The mold survives this process and can be reused for future beams.\n\n<a href=\"handbook://block-stonesupportbeam:stonesupportbeam-granite\">Stone support beams</a> can be crafted using 20 stone variants and 14 ashlar variants, matching whichever variant of rubble concrete you produced.\n\nHalite, Chalk, Claystone, Bauxite, Kimberlite, Obsidian, and Shale variants (plus Chalk, Claystone, Bauxite, and Shale ashlar) are included too. Some of these stone types are too brittle or crumbly to realistically hold up as structural beams, so if you prefer a more realistic selection, set \"includeAllStoneTypes\" to false in the mod's config file (stonesupportbeamconfig.json). The listed types are then removed, along with their crafting recipes and intermediate items."
}